2	// `if old is MISSING:`), is rewritten to None for the typed build, which has no object() values:
3	//
4	//     MISSING = object()                    pass
5	//     log.append((k, d.get(k, MISSING)))    log.append((k, d.get(k, None)))
6	//     if old is MISSING:            ->      if old is None:
7	//
8	// That keeps CPython's answers only when no value the program tests could be either one, so the rewrite is
9	// refused unless:
10	// - the name is set once, at the top level, and is only compared with `is`, `is not`, `==` or `!=`, passed
11	//   on and stored (never printed, called, indexed or read an attribute of);
12	// - every None test either pairs with the sentinel's own test on the same name (`v is MISSING or v is None`,
13	//   `v is not MISSING and v is not None`), where the two read the same after the rewrite, or tests a re
14	//   call (`re.match(...) is not None`), which never gives the sentinel;
15	// - no name the sentinel may reach (one tested against it, set from an expression naming it, or a
16	//   parameter defaulting to it) is tested for truth, where object() is true and None is false.
17	// Lines keep their numbers, so errors name the same lines.
